60,3,1,talk,Mio,,Option A is the flat fee. It is simple and covers our fixed costs.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,Option B is tiered. It might address the fear of full commitment.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Takumi,,Option C is activity-based. It feels fairer for those who do more.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Toshio,,I am against C. The hours logged prove it is unsustainable for the treasurer.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"I worry B might create friction, like the old named grades did.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@Toshio, if C is too hard, and B is risky, A seems safest.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Mio, but A might scare off the tasters who don't want a yearly commitment.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Jonathan, the tasters said they don't want a whole year at once. A flat fee is exactly that.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, that is a valid point. But the administrative cost of C is too high.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Mio, if we go with A, we need to make sure the price is reasonable.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Mio,,I think A is the best balance. It is predictable and covers the bills.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"I am still worried about the hesitation, but A is the most stable.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Takumi,,"I would prefer B, but I see the risk of friction.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Toshio,,I vote for A. It minimizes the work for the next treasurer.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Kenji,,I will go with A. It keeps the door open without complex calculations.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
